  "story": {
    "whatTitle": "What this is",
    "whatBody": "The AI Rishi is my public learning system. I learn, practice, debug, write it down, and teach from that. Teaching is how I check whether I actually understood the thing. The brand name is the long-term direction. The work on this site today is DevOps.",
    "whyTitle": "Why DevOps before AI",
    "whyBody": "AI can generate code, YAML, and commands. Someone still has to read the output, catch the lie, run it, and live with the failure. That someone needs Linux, Git, networking, DNS, HTTP, TLS, processes, logs, CI, containers, Kubernetes, identity, and the habit of proving claims with evidence. The goal is not to hide from AI. The goal is to use it from a position of understanding. I will not promise that this makes anyone unreplaceable, and I will not sell a job.",
    "methodTitle": "What you actually do",
    "methodBody": "A day is not a video. Read the lesson, predict, try without AI first, run it, break one thing safely, write the evidence, then review. If you cannot answer what fails, how you troubleshoot it, the trade-offs, and how it would land on this capstone, you covered the topic — you do not own it.",
    "pathTitle": "Where this is going",
    "pathBody": "DevOps is the current program. AI is next, after the foundation. Agentic AI comes after that. Those later stages stay off this site until there is real material to publish.",
    "communityTitle": "If you want to learn with me",
    "communityBody": "I am doing the hours too. If you are willing to practice, break things, and write evidence, you are welcome. I may help with doubts and debugging when the question shows real work. I am not running a certificate mill. Content on this site is free."
  },
